{
  "title": "8: al-Anfaal الأنفال",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْاَنْفَالِ ؕ قُلِ الْاَنْفَالُ لِلّٰهِ وَالرَّسُوْلِ ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَصْلِحُوْا ذَاتَ بَيْنِكُمْ وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(1)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AL-AANFAALE QOLIL AL-AANFAALU LILLAAHE WA RASOOLE FA TAQUL LAAHA WAASLEHOOA ZAATA BAYNAKUM WAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nThey ask thee concerning (things taken as) spoils of war. Say: “(such) spoils are at the disposal of Allah and the Messenger: So fear Allah, and keep straight the relations between yourselves: Obey Allah and His Messenger, if ye do believe.” \nاِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَجِلَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَاِذَا تُلِيَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُهٗ زَادَتْهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَّعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(2)\nINNAMAA MOAMENOONA LAZEENA EZAA ZUKERA LAAHO WAJELAT QULOOBUHUM WA EZAA TULEET A’LAYHIM AAYAATOHU ZAADATHUM EEMAANAW WWAA’ALAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nFor, Believers are those who, when Allah is mentioned, feel a tremor in their hearts, and when they hear His signs rehearsed, find their faith strengthened, and put (all) their trust in their Lord; \nالَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM ZAA YUNFEQOON.\nWho establish regular prayers and spend (freely) out of the gifts We have given them for sustenance: \nاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَقًّا ؕ لَهُمْ دَرَجٰتٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌۚ‏(4)\nAOOLAAEKA HOMUL MOAMENOONA HAQQAN LAHUM DARAJAATUN I’NDAL RABBEHIM WAMAGHFERATUN WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nSuch in truth are the believers: they have grades of dignity with their Lord, and forgiveness, and generous sustenance: \nكَمَاۤ اَخْرَجَكَ رَبُّكَ مِنْۢ بَيْتِكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّ فَرِيْقًا مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ لَكٰرِهُوْنَۙ‏(5)\nKAMAA AAKHRAJAKA RABBOKA MIN BAYTEKA BIL-HAQQE WA INNA FAREEQAM MENAL MOAMENEEN LAKAAREHOONA.\nJust as thy Lord ordered thee out of thy house in truth, even though a party among the Believers disliked it, \nيُجَادِلُوْنَكَ فِى الْحَقِّ بَعْدَ مَا تَبَيَّنَ كَاَنَّمَا يُسَاقُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَوْتِ وَهُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَؕ‏(6)\nYUJAADELOONAKA FIL HAQQE BA’DA MAA TABAYYANA KA-ANNAMAA YUSAAQOONA ELAL MAWT WA HUM YANZOROON.\nDisputing with thee concerning the truth after it was made manifest, as if they were being driven to death and they (actually) saw it. \nوَاِذْ يَعِدُكُمُ اللّٰهُ اِحْدَى الطَّآئِفَتَيْنِ اَنَّهَا لَكُمْ وَتَوَدُّوْنَ اَنَّ غَيْرَ ذَاتِ الشَّوْكَةِ تَكُوْنُ لَكُمْ وَيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّحِقَّ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَيَقْطَعَ دَابِرَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(7)\nWA IZ YA-E’DOKOMUL LAAHO EHDAB AT-TAAEFATAYNE AANNAHAA LAKUM WATAWADDOONA ANNAL GHAYRA ZAATIL ASH-SHAWKATE TAKOONO LAKUM WA YOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUHEQQA HAQQA BEKALEMAATEH WAYAQTAA’A DAABERA KAAFEREEN.\nBehold! Allah promised you one of the two (enemy) parties, that it should be yours: Ye wished that the one unarmed should be yours, but Allah willed to justify the Truth according to His words and to cut off the roots of the Unbelievers;- \nلِيُحِقَّ الْحَقَّ وَيُبْطِلَ الْبَاطِلَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَۚ‏(8)\nLEEHEQQA HAQQA WAYUBTELA AL-BAATELA WA LAW KAREHA MUJREMOON.\nThat He might justify Truth and prove Falsehood false, distasteful though it be to those in guilt. \nاِذْ تَسْتَغِيْثُوْنَ رَبَّكُمْ فَاسْتَجَابَ لَكُمْ اَنِّىْ مُمِدُّكُمْ بِاَلْفٍ مِّنَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ مُرْدِفِيْنَ‏(9)\nIZ TASTAGHEESOONA TAQUL FAASTAJAABA LAKUM AANNEAA MUMEDDUKUM BEAALFIN MENAL AL-MALAAEKATE MURDEFEENA.\nRemember ye implored the assistance of your Lord, and He answered you: “I will assist you with a thousand of the angels, ranks on ranks.” \nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بُشْرٰى وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ بِهٖ قُلُوْبُكُمْۚ وَمَا النَّصْرُ اِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(10)\nWA MAA JAA’ALAHU LAAHO ILLAA BUSHRAA WALETATMAENNA BEHI QOLOOBOKUM WA MAA AN-NASRU ILLAA MIN I’NDIL LAAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAllah made it but a message of hope, and an assurance to your hearts: (in any case) there is no help except from Allah: and Allah is Exalted in Power, Wise. \nاِذْ يُغَشِّيْكُمُ النُّعَاسَ اَمَنَةً مِّنْهُ وَيُنَزِّلُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً لِّيُطَهِّرَكُمْ بِهٖ وَيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمْ رِجْزَ الشَّيْطٰنِ وَلِيَرْبِطَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتَ بِهِ الْاَقْدَامَؕ‏(11)\nIZ YUGHASSHEEKUMU AN-NUA’AASA AAMANATAN MINHO WAYUNAZZELU A’LAYKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN LLEETAHHERAKUM BEHI WAYUZHEBA A’NKUM REJZA SHAYTAANE WALEERBETA A’LAA QOLOOBEKUM WAYUSABBETA BEHIL AL-AAQDAAMA.\nRemember He covered you with a sort of drowsiness, to give you calm as from Himself, and he caused rain to descend on you from heaven, to clean you therewith, to remove from you the stain of Satan, to strengthen your hearts, and to plant your feet firmly therewith. \nاِذْ يُوْحِىْ رَبُّكَ اِلَى الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اَنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ فَثَبِّتُوا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ سَاُلْقِىْ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعْبَ فَاضْرِبُوْا فَوْقَ الْاَعْنَاقِ وَاضْرِبُوْا مِنْهُمْ كُلَّ بَنَانٍؕ‏(12)\nIZ YOOHEAA RABBOKA ELAL AL-MALAAEKATE AANNEAA MA-A’KUM FASABBETOOA LAZEENA AAMANOO SAALQEAA FEE QOLOOBIL LAZEENA KAFARUL ROA’BA FAAZREBOOA FAWQA AL-AAA’NAAQE WAAZREBOOA MINHUM KULLA BANAANIN.\nRemember thy Lord inspired the angels (with the message): “I am with you: give firmness to the Believers: I will instil terror into the hearts of the Unbelievers: smite ye above their necks and smite all their finger-tips off them.” \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ شَآ قُّوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّشَاقِقِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(13)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM SHAA QQOOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA MAN YYUSHAAQEQE LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA-INNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nThis because they contended against Allah and His Messenger: If any contend against Allah and His Messenger, Allah is strict in punishment. \nذٰ لِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوْهُ وَاَنَّ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابَ النَّارِ‏(14)\nZAA ZAALEKUM FAZOOQOOHU WA ANNAL LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAL NAAR.\nThus (will it be said): “Taste ye then of the (punishment): for those who resist Allah, is the penalty of the Fire.” \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا لَقِيْتُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا زَحْفًا فَلَا تُوَلُّوْهُمُ الْاَدْبَارَۚ‏(15)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA LAQEETUMU LAZEENA KAFAROO ZAHFAN FALAA TOOLLOOHUMU ADBAAR.\nO ye who believe! when ye meet the Unbelievers in hostile array, never turn your backs to them. \nوَمَنْ يُّوَلِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ دُبُرَهٗۤ اِلَّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِّقِتَالٍ اَوْ مُتَحَيِّزًا اِلٰى فِئَةٍ فَقَدْ بَآءَ بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاْوٰٮهُ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(16)\nWA MAN YYOOLLEHEM YAWMA-EZIN DUBURAH ILLAA MUTAHARREFAN LLEQETAALIN AW MUTAHAYZAN ELAA FE-ATIN FAQAD BAAA BE-GHAZABIM MENAL LAAHE WAMAAWAAHU JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nIf any do turn his back to them on such a day - unless it be in a stratagem of war, or to retreat to a troop (of his own)- he draws on himself the wrath of Allah, and his abode is Hell, an evil refuge (indeed)! \nفَلَمْ تَقْتُلُوْهُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَتَلَهُمْ وَمَا رَمَيْتَ اِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَ لٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَمٰى ۚ وَلِيُبْلِىَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ مِنْهُ بَلَاۤءً حَسَنًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(17)\nFALAM TAQTULOOHUM LAAKINNAL LAAHA QATALAHUM WA MAA RAMAYTA IZ RAMAYTA WA LAAKENNA LAAHA RAMAA WALEEBLEAAA MOAMENEEN MINHO BALAAAN HASANAN INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nIt is not ye who slew them; it was Allah: when thou threwest (a handful of dust), it was not thy act, but Allah's: in order that He might test the Believers by a gracious trial from Himself: for Allah is He Who heareth and knoweth (all things). \nذٰ لِكُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُوْهِنُ كَيْدِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(18)\nZAA ZAALEKUM WA ANNAL LAAHA MOOHENU KAYDE KAAFEREEN.\nThat, and also because Allah is He Who makes feeble the plans and stratagem of the Unbelievers. \nاِنْ تَسْتَفْتِحُوْا فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الْفَتْحُۚ وَاِنْ تَنْتَهُوْا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْۚ وَ اِنْ تَعُوْدُوْا نَعُدْۚ وَلَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْكُمْ فِئَتُكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَوْ كَثُرَتْۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(19)\nIN TASTAFTEHOOA FAQAD JAAAKUMU AL-FATHU WA LA-NAR- FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA IN TAU’OODOOA NAU’UD WA LAN TUGHNEAAA A’NKUM FEATUKUM SHAY-ANW WA LAW KASURAT WA ANNAL LAAHA LAAHA MOAMENEEN.\n(O Unbelievers!) if ye prayed for victory and judgment, now hath the judgment come to you: if ye desist (from wrong), it will be best for you: if ye return (to the attack), so shall We. Not the least good will your forces be to you even if they were multiplied: for verily Allah is with those who believe! \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَا تَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ وَاَنْتُمْ تَسْمَعُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(20)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAA TAWALLAW A’NHO WA ANTUM TASMA-O’ON.\nO ye who believe! Obey Allah and His Messenger, and turn not away from him when ye hear (him speak). \nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO TAKOONOO QAALOO SAMEA’NAA WA HUM LAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nNor be like those who say, “We hear,” but listen not: \nاِنَّ شَرَّ الدَّوَآبِّ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الصُّمُّ الْبُكْمُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(22)\nINNAL SHARRA AD-DAWAABBE I’NDAL LAAHE AS-SUMMU AL-BUKMU LAZEENA LAA YA’QELOON.\n For the worst of beasts in the sight of Allah are the deaf and the dumb, those who understand not. \nوَلَوْ عَلِمَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِمْ خَيْرًا لَّاَسْمَعَهُمْؕ وَلَوْ اَسْمَعَهُمْ لَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA LAW A’LEMA LAAHO FEEHIM KHAYRAN LLAASMAA’AHUM WA LAW AASMAA’AHUM LATAWALLAWA WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nIf Allah had found in them any good. He would indeed have made them listen: (As it is), if He had made them listen, they would but have turned back and declined (Faith). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اسْتَجِيْبُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَلِلرَّسُوْلِ اِذَا دَعَاكُمْ لِمَا يُحْيِيْكُمْۚ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحُوْلُ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَقَلْبِهٖ وَاَنَّهٗۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT ASTAJEEBOOA LILLAAHE WA LIRRASOOLE EZAA DA-A’AKUM LEMAKH YOHYEEKUM WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YAHOOLU BAYNA MAR-E WA QALBEHI WA ANNAHU ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nO ye who believe! give your response to Allah and His Messenger, when He calleth you to that which will give you life; and know that Allah cometh in between a man and his heart, and that it is He to Whom ye shall (all) be gathered. \nوَاتَّقُوْا فِتْنَةً لَّا تُصِيْبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْكُمْ خَآصَّةً ۚ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(25)\nWAT TAQOO FETNATAN LAA TUSEEBANNA LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINKUM KHAASSATAN WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nAnd fear tumult or oppression, which affecteth not in particular (only) those of you who do wrong: and know that Allah is strict in punishment. \nوَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ اَنْتُمْ قَلِيْلٌ مُّسْتَضْعَفُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ تَخَافُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَخَطَّفَكُمُ النَّاسُ فَاٰوٰٮكُمْ وَاَيَّدَكُمْ بِنَصْرِهٖ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nWA KOROO IZ ANTUM QALEELUN MMUSTAZA’AFOONA FIL ARZE TAKHAAFOONA AN YYATAKHATTAFAKUMU NAASO FAAWAAKUM WAAYYADAKUM BENASREH WARAZAQAKUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nCall to mind when ye were a small (band), despised through the land, and afraid that men might despoil and kidnap you; But He provided a safe asylum for you, strengthened you with His aid, and gave you Good things for sustenance: that ye might be grateful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَخُوْنُوا اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ وَتَخُوْنُوْۤا اَمٰنٰتِكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(27)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAKHOONOOA LAAHA WA YATTABE-U’R WATAKHOONOOA AAMAANAATEKUM WA ANTUM TA’LAMOON.\nO ye that believe! betray not the trust of Allah and the Messenger, nor misappropriate knowingly things entrusted to you. \nوَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَاۤ اَمْوَالُكُمْ وَاَوْلَادُكُمْ فِتْنَةٌ  ۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(28)\nWA’ LAMOO ANNAMAA AMWAALOKUM WA LAA AWLAADOKUM FITNATUN WA ANNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd know ye that your possessions and your progeny are but a trial; and that it is Allah with Whom lies your highest reward. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تَتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ يَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ فُرْقَانًا وَّيُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْؕ وَ اللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(29)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TATTAQOOA LAAHA YAJ-A’L LAKUM FURQAANAN WWAYUKAFFER A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WA YAGHFIR LAKUM WA LAAHO ZUL FAZLIL A’ZEEM.\nO ye who believe! if ye fear Allah, He will grant you a criterion (to judge between right and wrong), remove from you (all) evil (that may afflict) you, and forgive you: for Allah is the Lord of grace unbounded. \nوَاِذْ يَمْكُرُ بِكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِيُثْبِتُوْكَ اَوْ يَقْتُلُوْكَ اَوْ يُخْرِجُوْكَؕ وَيَمْكُرُوْنَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللّٰهُؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرُ الْمٰكِرِيْنَ‏(30)\nWA IZ YAMKURU BEKA LAZEENA KAFAROO LEESBETOOKA AW YAQTULOOKA AW YUKHREJOOKA WA YAMKOROON WAYAMKURU LAAH WAL LAAHO KHAYRUR AL-MAAKEREENA.\nRemember how the Unbelievers plotted against thee, to keep thee in bonds, or slay thee, or get thee out (of thy home). They plot and plan, and Allah too plans; but the best of planners is Allah. \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا قَالُوْا قَدْ سَمِعْنَا لَوْ نَشَآءُ لَقُلْنَا مِثْلَ هٰذَٓا ۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA QAALOO QAD SAMEA’NAA LAW NASHAAA-O LAQULNAA MISLA HAAZAAA IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWhen Our Signs are rehearsed to them, they say: “We have heard this (before): if we wished, we could say (words) like these: these are nothing but tales of the ancients.” \nوَاِذْ قَالُوا اللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَ هٰذَا هُوَ الْحَقَّ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ فَاَمْطِرْ عَلَيْنَا حِجَارَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اَوِ ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(32)\nWA IZ QAALUD AL-LAAHUMMA IN KAANA HAAZAA HOWA HAQQA MIN I’NDEK FAAMTER A’LAYNAA HEJAARATAN MENAL SAMAAA-E AWE’ E-ATENAA BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nRemember how they said: “O Allah if this is indeed the Truth from Thee, rain down on us a shower of stones form the sky, or send us a grievous penalty.” \nوَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَاَنْتَ فِيْهِمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA MAA KAANA LAAHO LEEA’AZZEBAHUM WA ANTA FEEHEM WA MAA KAANA LAAHO MUA’AZZEBAHUM WA HUM YASTAGHFEROONA.\nBut Allah was not going to send them a penalty whilst thou wast amongst them; nor was He going to send it whilst they could ask for pardon. \nوَمَا لَهُمْ اَلَّا يُعَذِّبَهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَهُمْ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَمَا كَانُوْۤا اَوْلِيَآءَهٗ ؕ اِنْ اَوْلِيَآؤُهٗۤ اِلَّا الْمُتَّقُوْنَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA LAHUM ALLAA YUA’AZZEBAHUMU LAAHO WA HUM YASUDDOONA A’NIL MASJEDIL HARAAME WA MAA KAANOO AAWLEEAAAAH IN AAWLEEAAAUH ILLAA MUTTAQOON LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nBut what plea have they that Allah should not punish them, when they keep out (men) from the sacred Mosque - and they are not its guardians? No men can be its guardians except the righteous; but most of them do not understand. \nوَمَا كَانَ صَلَاتُهُمْ عِنْدَ الْبَيْتِ اِلَّا مُكَآءً وَّتَصْدِيَةً  ؕ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA MAA KAANA SALAATUHUM I’NDAL BAYTE ILLAA MUKAAAN WWATASDEETAN FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROONA.\nTheir prayer at the House (of Allah) is nothing but whistling and clapping of hands: (Its only answer can be), “Taste ye the penalty because ye blasphemed.” \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ لِيَصُدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَسَيُنْفِقُوْنَهَا ثُمَّ تَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ حَسْرَةً ثُمَّ يُغْلَبُوْنَ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ يُحْشَرُوْنَۙ‏(36)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM LEESUDDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE FASAYUNFEQOONAHAA SUMMA TAKOONO A’LAYHIM HASRATAN SUMMA YUGHLABOONA WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ELAA JAHANNAMA YUHSHAROONA.\nThe Unbelievers spend their wealth to hinder (man) from the path of Allah, and so will they continue to spend; but in the end they will have (only) regrets and sighs; at length they will be overcome: and the Unbelievers will be gathered together to Hell;- \nلِيَمِيْزَ اللّٰهُ الْخَبِيْثَ مِنَ الطَّيِّبِ وَ يَجْعَلَ الْخَبِيْثَ بَعْضَهٗ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فَيَرْكُمَهٗ جَمِيْعًا فَيَجْعَلَهٗ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nLEEMEEZA LAAHO KHABEESA MENAL AT-TAYBE WA YAJA’ALA KHABEESA BAA’ZAH A’LAA ELAA FAYARKUMAH JAMEE-A’A FAYAJA’ALAH FEE JAHANNAM OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nIn order that Allah may separate the impure from the pure, put the impure, one on another, heap them together, and cast them into Hell. They will be the ones to have lost. \nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ يَّنْتَهُوْا يُغْفَرْ لَهُمْ مَّا قَدْ سَلَفَۚ وَاِنْ يَّعُوْدُوْا فَقَدْ مَضَتْ سُنَّتُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(38)\nQUL LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO IN YYANTAHOOA YUGHFAR LAHUM MAA QAD SALAFA WA YYAU’OODOOA FAQAD MAZAT SUNNATU AWWALEEN.\nSay to the Unbelievers, if (now) they desist (from Unbelief), their past would be forgiven them; but if they persist, the punishment of those before them is already (a matter of warning for them). \nوَقَاتِلُوْهُمْ حَتّٰى لَا تَكُوْنَ فِتْنَةٌ وَّيَكُوْنَ الدِّيْنُ كُلُّهٗ لِلّٰهِۚ فَاِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(39)\nWAQAATELOOHUM HATTAA LAA TAKOONA FITNATUN WA YAKOONAD DEENO KULLUH LILLAAHE FA-ENIN TAHAW FA-INNAL LAAHA BEMAA YA’MALOON BASEER.\nAnd fight them on until there is no more tumult or oppression, and there prevail justice and faith in Allah altogether and everywhere; but if they cease, verily Allah doth see all that they do. \nوَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَوْلٰٮكُمْؕ نِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰى وَنِعْمَ النَّصِيْرُ‏(40)\nWA TAWALLAW FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA MAWLAAKUM NE’MA AL-MAWLAA WA NE’MA AN-NASEERU.\nIf they refuse, be sure that Allah is your Protector - the best to protect and the best to help. \nوَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَاَنَّ لِلّٰهِ خُمُسَهٗ وَ لِلرَّسُوْلِ وَلِذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۙ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلٰى عَبْدِنَا يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعٰنِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(41)\nWA’ LAMOO ANNAMAA GHANEMTUM MIN SHAY-IN FA ANNAL LILLAAHE KHUMUSAH WA LELRRASOOLE WALEZIL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENE WAB SABEELE IN KUNTUM AAMANTUM BIL-LAAHE WA MAA ANZALNAA A’LAA A’BDENAA YAWMA AL-FURQAANE YAWMA AL-TAQAA AL-JAMA’AANE WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd know that out of all the booty that ye may acquire (in war), a fifth share is assigned to Allah, and to the Messenger, and to near relatives, orphans, the needy, and the wayfarer, if ye do believe in Allah and in the revelation We sent down to Our servant on the Day of Testing, the Day of the meeting of the two forces. For Allah hath power over all things. \nاِذْ اَنْتُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الْقُصْوٰى وَ الرَّكْبُ اَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْؕ وَلَوْ تَوَاعَدْتُّمْ لَاخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِى الْمِيْعٰدِۙ وَلٰكِنْ لِّيَقْضِىَ اللّٰهُ اَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُوْلًا ۙ لِّيَهْلِكَ مَنْ هَلَكَ عَنْۢ بَيِّنَةٍ وَّيَحْيٰى مَنْ حَىَّ عَنْۢ بَيِّنَةٍ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَسَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(42)\nIZ ANTUM BIL-U’UDWATE DUNYAA WA HUM BIL-U’UDWATE AL-QUSWAA WA AR-RAKBU MIN MENKUM WA LAW TAWAAA’ADTTUM LAAKHTALAFTUM FIL AL-MEEA’AADE WA LAAKIL LLEEQZEAAA LAAHO AMRAN KAANA MAF-O’OLAA LLEEHLEKA MAN HALAKA A’N BAYYENAH WWAYAHYAA MAN HAA A’N BAYYENAH WA INNA LAAHA LASAMEEA’UN A’LEEM.\nRemember ye were on the hither side of the valley, and they on the farther side, and the caravan on lower ground than ye. Even if ye had made a mutual appointment to meet, ye would certainly have failed in the appointment: But (thus ye met), that Allah might accomplish a matter already enacted; that those who died might die after a clear Sign (had been given), and those who lived might live after a Clear Sign (had been given). And verily Allah is He Who heareth and knoweth (all things). \nاِذْ يُرِيْكَهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ مَنَامِكَ قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَّلَوْ اَرٰٮكَهُمْ كَثِيْرًا لَّفَشِلْتُمْ وَلَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِى الْاَمْرِ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَلَّمَؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(43)\nIZ YUREEKAHUMU LAAHO FEE MANAAMEKA QALEELAA WA LAW AARAAKAHUM KASEERAA LLAFASHELTUM WALATANAAZAA’TUM FIL AL-AAMRE LAAKINNAL LAAHA SALLAMA INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nRemember in thy dream Allah showed them to thee as few: if He had shown them to thee as many, ye would surely have been discouraged, and ye would surely have disputed in (your) decision; but Allah saved (you): for He knoweth well the (secrets) of (all) hearts. \nوَ اِذْ يُرِيْكُمُوْهُمْ اِذِ الْتَقَيْتُمْ فِىْۤ اَعْيُنِكُمْ قَلِيْلًا وَّيُقَلِّلُكُمْ فِىْۤ اَعْيُنِهِمْ لِيَقْضِىَ اللّٰهُ اَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُوْلًا ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(44)\nWA IZ YUREEKUMOOHUM EZIM AL-TAQAYTUM FEE AAA’YUNEKUM QALEELAA WWAYUQALLELUKUM FEE A’LAA LEEQZEAAA LAAHO AMRAN KAANA MAF-O’OLAA WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nAnd remember when ye met, He showed them to you as few in your eyes, and He made you appear as contemptible in their eyes: that Allah might accomplish a matter already enacted. For to Allah do all questions go back (for decision). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا لَقِيْتُمْ فِئَةً فَاثْبُتُوْا وَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَۚ‏(45)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA LAQEETUM FE-ATAN FAASBUTOOA WAZ KORUL LAAHA KASEERAA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO ye who believe! When ye meet a force, be firm, and call Allah in remembrance much (and often); that ye may prosper: \nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَا تَنَازَعُوْا فَتَفْشَلُوْا وَتَذْهَبَ رِيْحُكُمْ وَاصْبِرُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَۚ‏(46)\nWAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAA TANAAZAU’OOA FATAFSHALOOA WATAZHABA REEHUKUM WAASBEROOA INNAL LAAHA LAAHA MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nAnd obey Allah and His Messenger; and fall into no disputes, lest ye lose heart and your power depart; and be patient and persevering: For Allah is with those who patiently persevere: \nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ خَرَجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ بَطَرًا وَّرِئَآءَ النَّاسِ وَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(47)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO TAKOONOO KHARAJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM BATARAN WWAREAAA NAASE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAH WAL LAAHO BEMAA YA’MALOON MOHEETUM.\nAnd be not like those who started from their homes insolently and to be seen of men, and to hinder (men) from the path of Allah: For Allah compasseth round about all that they do. \nوَاِذْ زَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ وَقَالَ لَا غَالِبَ لَكُمُ الْيَوْمَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَاِنِّىْ جَارٌ لَّكُمْۚ فَلَمَّا تَرَآءَتِ الْفِئَتٰنِ نَكَصَ عَلٰى عَقِبَيْهِ وَقَالَ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّنْكُمْ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى مَا لَا تَرَوْنَ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اللّٰهَؕ وَاللّٰهُ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(48)\nWA IZ ZAYNA LAHOMUL SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM WA QAALA LAA GHAALEBA LAKOMUL YAWMA MENAL NAASE WA INNEE JAARUN LAKUM FALAMMAA TARAAATE AL-FEATAANE NAKASA A’LAA A’LAA WA QAALA INNEE BAREEE-UM MINKUM INNEE AARAA MAA LAA TARAWNA INNEE AKHAAFO LAAH WAL LAAHO SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nRemember Satan made their (sinful) acts seem alluring to them, and said: “No one among men can overcome you this day, while I am near to you”: But when the two forces came in sight of each other, he turned on his heels, and said: “Lo! I am clear of you; lo! I see what ye see not; Lo! I fear Allah: for Allah is strict in punishment.” \nاِذْ يَقُوْلُ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ وَالَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ غَرَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ دِيْنُهُمْؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(49)\nIZ YAQOOLO MONAAFEQOONA WAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN GHARRA HAAOOLAAA-E DEENUHUM WA MAN YYATAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAHE FA-INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nLo! the hypocrites say, and those in whose hearts is a disease: “These people, their religion has misled them.” But if any trust in Allah, behold! Allah is Exalted in might, Wise. \nوَ لَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ يَتَوَفَّى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا ۙ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَضْرِبُوْنَ وُجُوْهَهُمْ وَاَدْبَارَهُمْۚ وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(50)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ YATAWAFFAA LAZEENA KAFARUL TAHMELOHUL YAZREBOONA WUJOOHAHUM WAADBAARAHUM WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\nIf thou couldst see, when the angels take the souls of the Unbelievers (at death), (How) they smite their faces and their backs, (saying): “Taste the penalty of the blazing Fire- \nذٰلِكَ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِۙ‏(51)\nZAALEKA BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEKUM WA ANNAL LAAHA LAYSA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\n“Because of (the deeds) which your (own) hands sent forth; for Allah is never unjust to His servants: \nكَدَاْبِ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(52)\nKADAABE AALE FIR-A’WNA WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE TOOFAANO LAAHO BEZUNOOBEHEM INNAL LAAHA QAWEAAAUN SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\n“(Deeds) after the manner of the people of Pharaoh and of those before them: They rejected the Signs of Allah, and Allah punished them for their crimes: for Allah is Strong, and Strict in punishment: \nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَمْ يَكُ مُغَيِّرًا نِّعْمَةً اَنْعَمَهَا عَلٰى قَوْمٍ حَتّٰى يُغَيِّرُوْا مَا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(53)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA LAM YAKU MUGHAYRAN NNEA’MATAN AANA’AMAHAA A’LAA QAWMIN HATTAA YUGHAYROOA MAA BE-ANFOSEHIM WA ANNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\n“Because Allah will never change the grace which He hath bestowed on a people until they change what is in their (own) souls: and verily Allah is He Who heareth and knoweth (all things).” \nكَدَاْبِ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ وَاَغْرَقْنَاۤ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ وَكُلٌّ كَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(54)\nKADAABE AALE FIR-A’WNA WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM FA AHLAKNAAHUM BEZUNOOBEHEM WAAGHRAQNAA AALA FIR-A’WNA KULLUN KAANOO ZAALEMEEN.\n(Deeds) after the manner of the people of Pharaoh and those before them”: They treated as false the Signs of their Lord: so We destroyed them for their crimes, and We drowned the people of Pharaoh: for they were all oppressors and wrong-doers. \nاِنَّ شَرَّ الدَّوَآبِّ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(55)\nINNAL SHARRA AD-DAWAABBE I’NDAL LAAHE LAZEENA KAFAROO FAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nFor the worst of beasts in the sight of Allah are those who reject Him: They will not believe. \nاَلَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدْتَّ مِنْهُمْ ثُمَّ يَنْقُضُوْنَ عَهْدَهُمْ فِىْ كُلِّ مَرَّةٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(56)\nLAZEENA A’AAHADTTA MINHUM SUMMA YANQOZOONA A’AHDAHUM FEE KULLE MARRAH WA HUM LAA YATTAQOON.\nThey are those with whom thou didst make a covenant, but they break their covenant every time, and they have not the fear (of Allah). \nفَاِمَّا تَثْقَفَنَّهُمْ فِى الْحَرْبِ فَشَرِّدْ بِهِمْ مَّنْ خَلْفَهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(57)\nFA-IMMAA TASQAFANNAHUM FIL AL-HARBE FASHARRED BEHIM MAN KHALFAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM YAZZAKKAROONA.\nIf ye gain the mastery over them in war, disperse, with them, those who follow them, that they may remember. \nوَاِمَّا تَخَافَنَّ مِنْ قَوْمٍ خِيَانَةً فَانْۢبِذْ اِلَيْهِمْ عَلٰى سَوَآءٍ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْخَآئِنِيْنَ‏(58)\nWA AMMAA TAKHAAFANNA MIN QAWMIN KHEEANATAN FAANBEZ ELAYHIM A’LAA SAWAAIN INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL AL-KHAAENEENA.\nIf thou fearest treachery from any group, throw back (their covenant) to them, (so as to be) on equal terms: for Allah loveth not the treacherous. \nوَلَا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا سَبَقُوْا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ لَا يُعْجِزُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAA YAHSABANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO SABAQOOA INNAHUM LAA YUA’JEZOONA.\nLet not the unbelievers think that they can get the better (of the godly): they will never frustrate (them). \nوَاَعِدُّوْا لَهُمْ مَّا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ قُوَّةٍ وَّمِنْ رِّبَاطِ الْخَيْلِ تُرْهِبُوْنَ بِهٖ عَدُوَّ اللّٰهِ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ وَاٰخَرِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْ ۚ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَهُمُ ۚ اَللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُهُمْؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ شَىْءٍ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ يُوَفَّ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(60)\nWAAE’EDDOOA LAHUM MAA ENIS TA-TA’TUM MIN QUWWATIN WA MIN RREBAATE AL-KHAYLE TURHEBOONA BEHI A’ADOO LAAHE WAA’ADOOKUM WA AAKHEREEN MIN DOONEHEM LAA TAA’LAMOONAHUMU ALLAAHO YAA’LAMUHUM WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN SHAY-IN FEE SABEELIL LAAHE YOOFFA ELAYKUM WA ANTUM LAA TUZLAMOON.\nAgainst them make ready your strength to the utmost of your power, including steeds of war, to strike terror into (the hearts of) the enemies, of Allah and your enemies, and others besides, whom ye may not know, but whom Allah doth know. Whatever ye shall spend in the cause of Allah, shall be repaid unto you, and ye shall not be treated unjustly. \nوَاِنْ جَنَحُوْا لِلسَّلْمِ فَاجْنَحْ لَهَا وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(61)\nWA JANAHOOA LELSSALME FAAJNAH LAHAA WA TAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAH INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\n But if the enemy incline towards peace, do thou (also) incline towards peace, and trust in Allah: for He is One that heareth and knoweth (all things). \nوَاِنْ يُّرِيْدُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْدَعُوْكَ فَاِنَّ حَسْبَكَ اللّٰهُؕ هُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَيَّدَكَ بِنَصْرِهٖ وَبِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(62)\nWA YYUREEDOOA AN YYAKHDAU’OOKA FA-INNAL HASBAKA LAAH HOWA LAZEE AAYDAKA BENASREH WA BIL-MOAMENEENA.\nShould they intend to deceive thee, verily Allah sufficeth thee: He it is That hath strengthened thee with His aid and with (the company of) the Believers; \nوَاَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوْبِهِمْؕ لَوْ اَنْفَقْتَ مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مَّاۤ اَلَّفْتَ بَيْنَ قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ اَلَّفَ بَيْنَهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(63)\nWAALLAFA BAYNA FEE LAW AANFAQTA MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A MAA AALLAFTA BAYNA QOLOOBEHIM LAAKINNAL LAAHA AALLAFA BAYNAHUM INNAHU A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAnd (moreover) He hath put affection between their hearts: not if thou hadst spent all that is in the earth, couldst thou have produced that affection, but Allah hath done it: for He is Exalted in might, Wise. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ حَسْبُكَ اللّٰهُ وَ مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(64)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO HASBUKA LAAHO WA MANIS ATTABAA’AKA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nO Prophet! sufficient unto thee is Allah, (unto thee) and unto those who follow thee among the Believers. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلَى الْقِتَالِ ؕ اِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ عِشْرُوْنَ صَابِرُوْنَ يَغْلِبُوْا مِائَتَيْنِ ۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ مِّائَةٌ يَّغْلِبُوْۤا اَ لْفًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(65)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO HARREZE MOAMENEEN A’LAL AL-QETAALE IN YYAKUN MINKUM E’ESHROONA SAABEROONA YAGHLEBOOA MEAATAYNE WA YYAKUN MINKUM MMEAATUN YYAGHLEBOOA AALFAN MENAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YAFQAHOON.\nO Prophet! rouse the Believers to the fight. If there are twenty amongst you, patient and persevering, they will vanquish two hundred: if a hundred, they will vanquish a thousand of the Unbelievers: for these are a people without understanding. \nاَلْئٰنَ خَفَّفَ اللّٰهُ عَنْكُمْ وَعَلِمَ اَنَّ فِيْكُمْ ضَعْفًاؕ فَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ مِّائَةٌ صَابِرَةٌ يَّغْلِبُوْا مِائَتَيْنِۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ اَلْفٌ يَّغْلِبُوْۤا اَلْفَيْنِ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَ اللّٰهُ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(66)\nAALAANA KHAFFAFA LAAHO A’NKUM WA A’LEMA ANNAL FEEKUM ZAA’FAN FA-IN YYAKUN MINKUM MMEAATUN SAABERATUN YYAGHLEBOOA MEAATAYNE WA YYAKUN MINKUM AALFUN YYAGHLEBOOA AALFAYNE BE-IZNIL LAAH WA LAAHO LAAHA MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nFor the present, Allah hath lightened your (task), for He knoweth that there is a weak spot in you: But (even so), if there are a hundred of you, patient and persevering, they will vanquish two hundred, and if a thousand, they will vanquish two thousand, with the leave of Allah: for Allah is with those who patiently persevere. \nمَا كَانَ لِنَبِىٍّ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ لَهٗۤ اَسْرٰى حَتّٰى يُثْخِنَ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ تُرِيْدُوْنَ عَرَضَ الدُّنْيَا ۖ  وَاللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(67)\nMAA KAANA LE-NABIYYIL AN YAKOONA LAHU AASRAA HATTAA YUSKHENA FIL ARZ TOREEDOONA A’ARAZA DUNYAA WAL LAAHO YOREEDO AAKHERATA WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nIt is not fitting for a prophet that he should have prisoners of war until he hath thoroughly subdued the land. Ye look for the temporal goods of this world; but Allah looketh to the Hereafter: And Allah is Exalted in might, Wise. \nلَوْلَا كِتٰبٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيْمَاۤ اَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(68)\nLAWLAA KETAABUM MENAL LAAHE SABAQA LAMASSAKUM FEEMAA AAKHAZTUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nHad it not been for a previous ordainment from Allah, a severe penalty would have reached you for the (ransom) that ye took. \nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا غَنِمْتُمْ حَلٰلاً طَيِّبًا ۖ  وَّاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(69)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA GHANEMTUM HALAALAAN TAYYEBAA WWAATTAQOOA LAAHA INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut (now) enjoy what ye took in war, lawful and good: but fear Allah: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ قُلْ لِّمَنْ فِىْۤ اَيْدِيْكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَسْرٰٓىۙ اِنْ يَّعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِكُمْ خَيْرًا يُّؤْتِكُمْ خَيْرًا مِّمَّاۤ اُخِذَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(70)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO QUL LEMAN FEE AYDEEKUM MENAL AL-AASRAAA IN YYAA’LAME LAAHO FEE QOLOOBEKUM KHAYRAN YYUTEKUM KHAYRAN MIMMAA AUKHEZA MINKUM WA YAGHFIR LAKUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO Prophet! say to those who are captives in your hands: “If Allah findeth any good in your hearts, He will give you something better than what has been taken from you, and He will forgive you: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful.” \nوَاِنْ يُّرِيْدُوْا خِيَانَتَكَ فَقَدْ خَانُوا اللّٰهَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَاَمْكَنَ مِنْهُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(71)\nWA YYUREEDOOA KHEEANATAKA FAQAD KHAANOOA LAAHA MIN QABLO FAAMKANA MINHUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nBut if they have treacherous designs against thee, (O Messenger!), they have already been in treason against Allah, and so hath He given (thee) power over them. And Allah so He Who hath (full) knowledge and wisdom. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰوَوْا وَّنَصَرُوْۤا اُولٰۤئِكَ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَمْ يُهَاجِرُوْا مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ وَّلَايَتِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ حَتّٰى يُهَاجِرُوْا ۚ وَاِنِ اسْتَنْصَرُوْكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِ فَعَلَيْكُمُ النَّصْرُ اِلَّا عَلٰى قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(72)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA AAAWAWA WWANASAROOA AOOLAAEKA KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z WA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA LAM YUHAAJEROOA MAA LAKUM MIN WWALAAYATEHEM MIN SHAY-IN HATTAA YUHAAJEROOA WA ENIS ASTANSAROOKUM FIL DEENE FA A’LAYKOMUL AN-NASRU ILLAA A’LAA QAWMIN BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MMEESAAQUN WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nThose who believed, and adopted exile, and fought for the Faith, with their property and their persons, in the cause of Allah, as well as those who gave (them) asylum and aid, these are (all) friends and protectors, one of another. As to those who believed but came not into exile, ye owe no duty of protection to them until they come into exile; but if they seek your aid in religion, it is your duty to help them, except against a people with whom ye have a treaty of mutual alliance. And (remember) Allah seeth all that ye do. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ اِلَّا تَفْعَلُوْهُ تَكُنْ فِتْنَةٌ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَفَسَادٌ كَبِيْرٌؕ‏(73)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z WA ILLAA TAFA’ALOOHU TAKUN FITNATUN FIL ARZE WAFASAADUN KABEERUN.\nThe Unbelievers are protectors, one of another: Unless ye do this, (protect each other), there would be tumult and oppression on earth, and great mischief. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجٰهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَاوَوْا وَّنَصَرُوْۤا اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَقًّا ؕ لَّهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(74)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WAJAAHADOOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA AAAWAWA WWANASAROOA AOOLAAEKA HOMUL MOAMENOONA HAQQAN LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nThose who believe, and adopt exile, and fight for the Faith, in the cause of Allah as well as those who give (them) asylum and aid, these are (all) in very truth the Believers: for them is the forgiveness of sins and a provision most generous. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدُ وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا مَعَكُمْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ مِنْكُمْؕ وَاُولُوا الْاَرْحَامِ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلٰى بِبَعْضٍ فِىْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(75)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MIN BA’DO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO MA-A’KUM FAAWLAAEKA MENKUM WA ULUL AL-AARHAAME KHALAA AAWLAA BE-BA’Z FEE KETAABIL LAAH INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAnd those who accept Faith subsequently, and adopt exile, and fight for the Faith in your company, they are of you. But kindred by blood have prior rights against each other in the Book of Allah. Verily Allah is well-acquainted with all things. ",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Madinah and it has 75 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayaan, it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah al-Anfaal and [Surah al-Tawba](A13) every month, he will be protected from being a hypocrite and will be counted among the followers of Ameerul Momineen – Imam Ali (a.s.), and on the day of Qiyamah he will eat from the table-spread of Jannah together with all the followers of Ahlul Bayt.\nThis Surah contains the verse about khums, which is the right of the Ahlul Bayt. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that he will, on the Day of Judgement, intercede for the person who recites this Surah and will bear witness that the reciter of this Surah was free from hypocrisy. Keeping Surah al-Anfaal in your possession at all times ensures that you get your rights that have been taken from you and your legitimate desires are fulfilled."
